    "plain_text": "Internet calling extended Donald Burns's telecommunications work beyond traditional phone services. He served as president and subsequently chairman of YMax, then joined the board of magicJack, whose technology connected telephone calls through broadband internet. As magicJack chairman from 2013, he brought experience of leading a public telecommunications business to its board. Burns had attended the University of Maryland before building his business career.\n\nThrough the Donald A. Burns Foundation, he established a separate channel for charitable giving. He continues to serve as its president, overseeing a grantmaking organisation based in Palm Beach. Its work has supported educational opportunities, medical services, and arts and humanities organisations.",
